    "detailed_description": "<h1>MORE FROM YYM - A GAME ABOUT DONUTS \ud83c\udf69</h1><p></p><br><h1>Physical Merchandise</h1><p><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/460430/extras/cdf6e785ae20f64acc89912178a420a7.avif?t=1750671123\" /></div><br><br>In love with the game? You can purchase The Letter physical goodies through our webstore! Our <strong>Collector's Edition</strong> is a must-have for every fan!<br><br><br><br>Thank you so much for your support! All proceeds will go towards our future games!</p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">CONTENT WARNING</h2>This game deals with mature themes. It shows scenes that some may find disturbing, unethical and triggering. It also contains offensive language, racial slurs, sexual themes, gore and violence. Player discretion is advised. For the full list of trigger warnings, please check our Steam forums.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">ABOUT</h2>The Letter is an interactive, horror/drama visual novel inspired by classic Asian horror films, Ju-ON: The Grudge and The Ring. Told through an immersive branching narrative, the game puts the players into the shoes of seven characters as they find themselves falling prey to a vicious curse plaguing the Ermengarde Mansion for centuries. <br><br><br>In this game, your choices will shape and drive the story forward: will you mend a relationship on the verge of collapse, or will you let it fall apart? Will you risk saving them, despite the consequences, or leave them to die a gruesome death? The fate of all the characters is in your hands.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">FEATURES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>This is a hardcore visual novel with over 700K words. Expect <i>a lot</i> of reading!<br></li><li>Romance, friendship and drama; apart from horror, the game puts heavy emphasis on relationships and character development.<br></li><li>Non-chronological storytelling with 7 playable characters, each with varying personality and approach to difficult situations.<br></li><li>Countless butterfly effects; your choices heavily affect the story.<br></li><li>Full English Voice Acting (optional).<br></li><li>Animated backgrounds, CGs and sprites.<br></li><li>Beautifully painted art style, with over 80 backgrounds, 100 CGs and 50 Epilogue CGs (variations included).<br></li><li>Original soundtrack, with opening, ending and true ending theme songs.<br></li><li>Quick-Time Events (optional).<br></li><li>A branching tree that keeps track of your progress/route.<br></li><li>A journal that narrates the events in chronological order, and jots down the clues found about the Ermengarde Mansion.<br></li><li>Over 170 achievements.</li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">CONTENT WARNING</h2>This game deals with mature themes. It shows scenes that some may find disturbing, unethical and triggering. It also contains offensive language, racial slurs, sexual themes, gore and violence. Player discretion is advised. For the full list of trigger warnings, please check our Steam forums.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">ABOUT</h2>The Letter is an interactive, horror/drama visual novel inspired by classic Asian horror films, Ju-ON: The Grudge and The Ring. Told through an immersive branching narrative, the game puts the players into the shoes of seven characters as they find themselves falling prey to a vicious curse plaguing the Ermengarde Mansion for centuries. <br><br><br>In this game, your choices will shape and drive the story forward: will you mend a relationship on the verge of collapse, or will you let it fall apart? Will you risk saving them, despite the consequences, or leave them to die a gruesome death? The fate of all the characters is in your hands.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">FEATURES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>This is a hardcore visual novel with over 700K words. Expect <i>a lot</i> of reading!<br></li><li>Romance, friendship and drama; apart from horror, the game puts heavy emphasis on relationships and character development.<br></li><li>Non-chronological storytelling with 7 playable characters, each with varying personality and approach to difficult situations.<br></li><li>Countless butterfly effects; your choices heavily affect the story.<br></li><li>Full English Voice Acting (optional).<br></li><li>Animated backgrounds, CGs and sprites.<br></li><li>Beautifully painted art style, with over 80 backgrounds, 100 CGs and 50 Epilogue CGs (variations included).<br></li><li>Original soundtrack, with opening, ending and true ending theme songs.<br></li><li>Quick-Time Events (optional).<br></li><li>A branching tree that keeps track of your progress/route.<br></li><li>A journal that narrates the events in chronological order, and jots down the clues found about the Ermengarde Mansion.<br></li><li>Over 170 achievements.</li></ul>",
    "short_description": "When seven people fall prey to a vicious curse, they will discover that horror rests not from the shadows lurking about, but within themselves. To what ends will one go in order to survive?",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cI do not hand out a review score of ten lightly. I've only ever given one, and this will be the second. I've thoroughly enjoyed my time with The Letter, and I am certain it is not over just yet.\u201d<br>10/10 \u2013 Rely on Horror<br><br>\u201cThe Letter is a terrifying labor of love, and I\u2019m incredibly grateful that I backed it.\u201d<br>Unwinnable<br><br>\u201cDid you ever get one of those chain text messages? During my high school years, they became so pervasive that they were more annoying than scary. Horror visual novel The Letter changes all that.\u201d<br>Kotaku<br>",
